    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I need some help drafting a performance review for one of my Senior Account Executives. Can you help me write something professional? \n\nBasically, they're doing a great job with client retention—clients really love them and our numbers are up. But, they're constantly late to our internal morning stand-up meetings, which is starting to annoy the rest of the team. I want to keep the tone constructive so they don't get discouraged, but I need to address the punctuality issue clearly.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For a performance review, you can start by highlighting their exceptional client management skills, like how they've successfully driven client retention and boosted revenue. You might phrase it like, \"\\[Name] has demonstrated outstanding success in client retention, consistently exceeding targets and building strong client relationships.\" Then, transition to the area for development by framing it as an opportunity for growth, rather than a failure. You could add, \"To further enhance their impact on the team, we need to focus on improving punctuality for our morning stand-ups.\" This balances praise with clear, actionable feedback.",
